Subject: GoldenEye levels: a guard sent to a pad on a wall stops off the wall, as in GoldenEye

GitHub issue 5 (Kode-Z): in Bunker 1 the guard who runs for the alarm "runs
around in circles" by it. Not a frame-rate bug: it circled at 30, 60 and 120
FPS on the clang oracle (M-059). The cause is a line of GoldenEye that the
conversion's guards never ran. GoldenEye's chrGoToPad() (the decomp's
chraction.c) sends a guard to a pad that does not face up - one
on a wall, as an alarm's, a console's or a keyboard's - not to the pad but to
the point 1.1 body widths out from it along its up vector, off the wall
(where GoldenEye's tile walk from the pad reaches that point; where it does
not, GoldenEye does not send him at all). Perfect Dark's chrGoToPad() goes to
the pad itself, and every GoldenEye RunToPad/WalkToPad/RunToPadPreset of a
converted mission comes through it.

Bunker 1's alarm is pad 127, up (-1, 0, 0), 5.7 units off its wall. Sent to the
pad, the guard came at it along the wall; chrNavCanSeeNextPos()'s side line,
1.2 widths off the route, then ends 18 inside the wall, the pad is never
"seen", the wall is taken for an obstacle and he is routed round its corner,
over and over, until one pass happens to come within 30 of the pad: 3 to 38 s.
On the GoldenEye decomp's own build of Bunker 1 (scratch, round 2 of D-117) the
same guard's target is the pad plus 22 along its up: GoldenEye's
coordinates (-1208.7, 3063.1) for a pad at (-1186.7, 3063.1), which is ours,
offset, to the unit. Sent there, the side line ends clear of the wall and he
runs to it: forced sighting, alarm 1.9 s after he starts at 30 and 60 FPS and
2.8 s at 120 (stock 11.2 and 22.4; GoldenEye 1.7).

Only on a level converted from GoldenEye (geRoomActive()) and only for a
GoldenEye chr (not a simulant); a pad that faces up is gone to as before, and
so is any pad where the tile graph cannot say (no graph, or no tile under the
pad). Perfect Dark's own levels never take the branch.

--- a/src/game/chraction.c
+++ b/src/game/chraction.c
@@ -8875,11 +8875,48 @@
 			RoomNum rooms[2];
 			struct pad pad;
 
-			padUnpack(padnum, PADFIELD_ROOM | PADFIELD_POS, &pad);
+			padUnpack(padnum, PADFIELD_ROOM | PADFIELD_POS
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+					| PADFIELD_UP
+#endif
+					, &pad);
 
 			rooms[0] = pad.room;
 			rooms[1] = -1;
 
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+			// (overlay 0065) On a level converted from GoldenEye, GoldenEye's
+			// own chrGoToPad(): a pad that does not face up - one on a wall,
+			// as an alarm's, a console's or a keyboard's is - is gone to 1.1
+			// body widths out along its up, off the wall, where the walk
+			// along the tile graph from the pad reaches; where it does not,
+			// GoldenEye does not go at all. Perfect Dark goes to the pad
+			// itself. Bunker 1's alarm (pad 127) is 5.7 from its wall, so
+			// the guard sent to it was sent into the wall's foot: the side
+			// lines of chrNavCanSeeNextPos() ended inside the wall, the pad
+			// was never "seen" and he circled the corner until a pass came
+			// within 30 of it (GitHub issue 5) - 3 to 38 s at every rate,
+			// where GoldenEye's own guard, sent 22 out, runs to it.
+			if (geRoomActive() && chr->aibot == NULL && pad.up.y < 0.5f) {
+				struct coord region;
+				s32 reaches;
+
+				region.x = pad.pos.x + pad.up.x * (chr->radius * 1.1f);
+				region.y = pad.pos.y + pad.up.y * (chr->radius * 1.1f);
+				region.z = pad.pos.z + pad.up.z * (chr->radius * 1.1f);
+
+				reaches = geStanWalkReaches(&pad.pos, region.x, region.z);
+
+				if (reaches == 1) {
+					return chrGoToRoomPos(chr, &region, rooms, goposflags);
+				}
+
+				if (reaches == 0) {
+					return false;
+				}
+			}
+#endif
+
 			if (chrGoToRoomPos(chr, &pad.pos, rooms, goposflags)) {
 				return true;
 			}
